    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey im seeing a CrashLoopBackOff on my auth-service pod in gke. logs show:\n`Error: Cannot find module '/app/dist/index.js' thrown by process`\nand then it just exits. i already checked the dockerfile and the entrypoint looks right. can u give me a checklist of what to look at to figure out if its a config issue or something else?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A `CrashLoopBackOff` with a missing module error, even when the Dockerfile looks right, is often a pathing or dependency issue. First, check if the build artifacts are actually present inside the running container image, perhaps by running a shell into the image. Then, verify that the working directory set in your deployment matches where the compiled JavaScript file is actually located. Finally, ensure that any necessary environment variables that might alter the application's runtime path are correctly passed to the pod.",
      "source": "target",
