    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah that makes sense. i'll check the initialDelaySeconds. i'm also wondering if there are other weird things that could cause this besides just config, like maybe some underlying issue with the node or the container runtime itself? what else should i be looking for if it's not an obvious misconfig?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If it's not a configuration error, you might be dealing with issues deeper in the infrastructure, which is always a possibility. You should check the node's logs using `kubectl describe node <node-name>` to see if there are any underlying kernel panics or resource starvation warnings. Also, examine the Kubernetes events for the pod using `kubectl describe pod <pod-name>` for any low-level runtime errors reported by the Kubelet. Sometimes, a very aggressive security policy (like an overly restrictive PodSecurityPolicy or NetworkPolicy) can interfere with the application's ability to start correctly, even if the image is sound.",
      "source": "target",
